{
  "category": "Crowd coding",
  "title": "Practice and gold units",
  "description": "Crowd coders sort made-up news headlines by topic and say whether they are clickbait. They start with 4 practice headlines that give feedback when an answer is wrong; the 12 headlines are divided among the crowd so that each is coded by two coders; 3 gold headlines with a known topic are spread among them, checked silently, and coders who get too many wrong are screened out. With example answers from 2 coders, one of whom got a gold headline wrong.",
  "tryThis": [
    "Open the link (Links page) in a private window and answer a practice headline wrongly: you see why, and answer again.",
    "Code on and get two gold headlines wrong in a row (the burglar, the unemployment figures, the swimming club): the study ends at the Screen-out branch's end item.",
    "See the right answers in the units: the columns answer_topic, feedback_topic, answer_clickbait and feedback_clickbait, and the column test_set with practice and gold (Units page). Coders never get these columns.",
    "Open the unit loop on the Design page: the headlines divided among coders (two per headline), practice units before them, gold units spread throughout, and the health that ends a session.",
    "See how each coder did on the test units in Results › Coders."
  ],
